[7.907475, "o", "rned that Ms Corwin may not appreciate that these stays violate the custodial order.\r\nST-515,addressee,mother,OI-201,This letter goes to counsel for Ms Corwin — the mother's attorney.\r\nST-516,addressee,father,CL-301,Address the letter to the father's attorney.\r\nST-517,addressee,father,OI-299,To counsel for Mr Adler.\r\nST-518,request,CL match,OI-208,Neither child overnight in her care unless the father is present.\r\nST-519,request,unless mother,CL-302,Neither child overnight in her care unless Ms Corwin is present.\r\nST-520,delivery,post,OI-204,Send it by post to counsel's office.\r\nST-521,delivery,email,CL-306,Send the letter by email to opposing counsel.\r\nST-522,delivery,courier,OI-299,Deliver by courier to counsel's office.\r\nST-523,copies,nobody,OI-205,Do not copy anyone on this letter.\r\nST-524,copies,copy father,CL-305,Copy: Mr Adler.\r\nST-525,enclosure,certified,OI-209,A certified copy of the custodial plan is enclosed.\r\nST-526,enclosure,unsigned,CL-303,An unsigned draft of the custodial plan is enclosed.\r\nS"]
[7.907783, "o", "T-527,salutation,Dear Counsel,OI-211,\"Dear Counsel,\"\r\nST-528,salutation,Dear Mr Adler,CL-304,\"Dear Mr Adler,\"\r\nST-529,children_named,both with ages,CL-301,\"This concerns Noor, aged seven, and Imogen, aged twelve.\"\r\nST-530,children_named,both no ages,OI-203,This concerns Noor and Imogen.\r\nST-531,children_named,Noor only,CL-304,\"This concerns Noor, aged seven.\"\r\nST-532,right_of_first_refusal,full,CL-306,\"Mr Adler agreed to a right of first refusal, so the children are not to be left overnight without him present.\"\r\nST-533,right_of_first_refusal,mother agreed,OI-202,\"Ms Corwin agreed to a right of first refusal, so the children are not to be left overnight without her present.\"\r\nST-534,right_of_first_refusal,agreement only no overnight,OI-202,Mr Adler agreed to a right of first refusal.\r\nST-535,overnight_stays,full,CL-302,On several occasions both children stayed overnight at her home or with a sitter while the father was away.\r\nST-536,overnight_stays,home only,OI-204,On several occasions both children stayed ov"]
[7.908677, "o", "ernight at Ms Corwin's home while Mr Adler was away.\r\nST-537,overnight_stays,one child,CL-301,On several occasions Imogen stayed overnight at her home or with a sitter while the father was away.\r\nST-538,inconsistent_accounts,all four,CL-303,\"Mr Adler has described Ms Corwin as his wife to the school, as the person Imogen lives with to her clinicians, as a babysitter to me, and as his partner to the neighbours.\"\r\nST-539,inconsistent_accounts,three no neighbour,OI-205,\"Mr Adler has described Ms Corwin as his wife to the school, as the person Imogen lives with to her clinicians, and as a babysitter to me.\"\r\nST-540,sender_signature,full name,CL-305,\"Yours sincerely, Delphine Marr.\"\r\nST-541,sender_signature,as counsel,OI-211,\"Yours sincerely, for Delphine Marr, solicitor.\"\r\nST-542,sender_signature,first name only,CL-302,\"Yours sincerely, Delphine.\"\r\nST-543,request,wording delivery,OI-208,Send it by post to counsel's office.\r\nST-544,tone,wording copies,OI-210,Do not copy anyone on this letter.\r\nST-545,concern,wordi"]
[7.908856, "o", "ng enclosure,CL-309,A certified copy of the custodial plan is enclosed.\r\nST-546,delivery,wording salutation,CL-306,\"Dear Counsel,\"\r\nST-547,behavioural_plan,wording addressee mother,OI-207,This letter goes to counsel for Ms Corwin — the mother's attorney.\r\nST-548,reply_deadline,7 days,OI-210,Please reply within seven days.\r\nST-549,reply_deadline,14 days,CL-307,A reply within fourteen days is requested.\r\nST-550,school_reference,principal,OI-205,The school principal can confirm the account.\r\nST-551,mediation_offer,open,CL-309,I remain willing to mediate.\r\nST-552,legal_fees,shared,OI-201,Legal fees will be shared equally.\r\nST-553,court_listing,directions,CL-306,List the matter for directions within 28 days.\r\nST-554,expert_report,joint,OI-207,I propose a joint expert on the overnight arrangements.\r\nST-555,interim_contact,supervised,CL-302,Interim contact should be supervised only.\r\nST-556,without_prejudice,mark letter,OI-211,This letter is sent without prejudice.\r\nST-557,hearing_bundle,bundle index enclosed,CL-3"]
[7.909642, "o", "01,A hearing bundle index is enclosed for the court.\r\nST-558,tone,firm formal brief,OI-201,\"Adopt a firm, formal and brief style.\"\r\nST-559,concern,position only,OI-299,I raise only the position she has been put in.\r\nST-560,behavioural_plan,full CL match,OI-299,\"The behavioural plan covers confidence, stability and peer relations; the stays have set back confidence only.\"\r\nST-561,interim_contact,all three aspects together,CL-308,\"Pending the final order, interim contact with Ms Corwin should be framed to support Imogen's confidence, her stability and her peer relations together.\"\r\nST-562,interim_contact,confidence stability peer relations jointly,CL-310,\"Any interim contact arrangement must work across all three pillars of the plan — confidence, stability and peer relations — rather than picking one alone.\"\r\nST-563,interim_contact,all three aspects jointly,OI-207,\"Interim contact pending resolution ought to hold confidence, stability and peer relations in view at the same time, because interim contact touc"]
[7.90984, "o", "hes each of them.\"\r\nST-564,interim_contact,all three addressed together,CL-310,\"Until the matter is resolved, contact with Ms Corwin must be arranged so that confidence, stability and peer relations are all addressed, not one in isolation.\"\r\nST-565,interim_contact,confidence stability peer relations all three,CL-308,\"The interim contact schedule should be built around confidence, stability and peer relations jointly, since interim contact bears on all three.\"\r\nST-566,interim_contact,confidence only,CL-308,\"Pending resolution, interim contact with Ms Corwin should be arranged to support Imogen's confidence.\"\r\nST-567,interim_contact,confidence the aspect set back,CL-308,\"Interim contact pending the final order need only address confidence, as that is the aspect the stays have set back.\"\r\nST-568,interim_contact,confidence above all,OI-207,\"Until the matter is resolved, contact with Ms Corwin should focus on confidence above all else.\"\r\nST-569,interim_contact,confidence the only aspect set back,CL-308,\"The interi"]
[7.909882, "o", "m contact schedule should be built around confidence, because that is the only aspect the stays have set back.\"\r\nST-570,interim_contact,confidence only despite citation,CL-310,\"Any interim contact arrangement pending resolution need only consider confidence, the aspect the stays affected.\"\r\nST-571,without_prejudice,soft conciliatory tone,CL-307,\"Without prejudice, I write in a conciliatory spirit to explore whether common ground can be found for the children's sake.\"\r\nST-572,without_prejudice,soft tone settlement offer,CL-311,\"Marked without prejudice, this letter is framed softly and without rancour, as befits a genuine attempt to settle.\"\r\nST-573,without_prejudice,conciliatory and open,OI-210,\"On a without prejudice basis, the tone here is deliberately gentle and conciliatory, inviting agreement rather than contest.\"\r\nST-574,without_prejudice,soft and measured,CL-307,\"Sent without prejudice, the letter adopts a soft and measured tone throughout, in keeping with its purpose as a settlement offer.\"\r\nST-575,wi"]
[7.909914, "o", "thout_prejudice,gentle settlement tone,CL-311,\"This without prejudice communication is written gently and without assertion, so as to keep the door open to resolution.\"\r\nST-576,without_prejudice,firm and direct,CL-307,\"Without prejudice, I set out the position firmly and directly, leaving no room for misunderstanding.\"\r\nST-577,without_prejudice,firm formal brief,CL-307,\"Marked without prejudice, the letter is firm, formal and brief in keeping with the tone the clarification requires.\"\r\nST-578,without_prejudice,firm and uncompromising,OI-210,\"On a without prejudice basis, the tone throughout is firm and uncompromising, as the client's instructions demand.\"\r\nST-579,without_prejudice,firm despite without prejudice,CL-311,\"Sent without prejudice, the position is stated firmly and without concession, though the label invites settlement.\"\r\nST-580,without_prejudice,firm formal and at length,CL-307,\"Without prejudice, I keep the letter firm, formal and at length, setting out every point in full detail.\"\r\nST-581,tone,"]
[7.910002, "o", "soft formal succinct,CL-309,\"The letter should be kept soft, formal and succinct throughout.\"\r\nST-582,tone,firm formal brief,CL-308,\"Set a firm, formal and brief tone throughout the letter.\"\r\nST-583,concern,both limbs,CL-307,\"It concerns me that Ms Corwin may not appreciate the stays violate the order, and I am also concerned about the position she has been placed in.\"\r\nST-584,concern,position only,CL-306,My concern is solely the position Ms Corwin has been placed in.\r\nST-585,behavioural_plan,confidence stability setback,CL-309,\"The behavioural plan is built around confidence and stability, and the stays have set that plan back.\"\r\nST-586,behavioural_plan,CL match confidence-only setback,CL-307,\"Her behavioural plan addresses confidence, stability and peer relations, and the stays have set back her confidence alone.\"\r\nST-587,addressee,father's attorney,CL-307,Please direct this letter to the attorney acting for the father.\r\nST-588,addressee,mother's attorney,CL-308,This letter is to be sent to counsel for the"]
[7.910136, "o", " mother.\r\nST-589,request,neither child overnight unless father present,CL-309,Neither child ought to stay overnight in Ms Corwin's care unless Mr Adler is present.\r\nST-590,request,unless mother present,CL-304,Neither child should stay overnight with her unless the mother is present.\r\nST-591,enclosure,certified copy,CL-306,Enclosed with this letter is a certified copy of the custodial plan.\r\nST-592,enclosure,uncertified summary,CL-307,Enclosed is an uncertified draft summary of the custodial plan.\r\nST-593,tone,warm and conversational,CL-305,The tone should be warm and conversational throughout.\r\nST-594,concern,both limbs,CL-303,\"I have a concern that she may not appreciate the stays contravene the order, as well as about the position she has been put in.\"\r\nST-595,behavioural_plan,no effect on plan,CL-302,The stays have had no effect on Imogen's behavioural plan.\r\n"]
