[16.994332, "o", "ST-103 | overnight_stays | several occasions at her home or with a sitter | OI-204 | On several occasions both children have stayed overnight at Ms Corwin's home or with a sitter while Mr Adler was away.\r\nST-104 | addressee | the father's attorney | OI-201 | To counsel for Mr Adler.\r\nST-105 | inconsistent_accounts | wife to the school, resident to clinicians, sitter to the sender | OI-205 | Mr Adler has described Ms Corwin as his wife to the school, as the person Imogen lives with to her clinicians, and as a babysitter to me.\r\nST-106 | concern | violation limb only | OI-206 | I am concerned that Ms Corwin may not appreciate that these stays violate the custodial order.\r\nST-107 | behavioural_plan | the stays have had no effect on the plan | OI-207 | Imogen's behavioural plan focuses on her confidence and stability, and the stays have not affected her progress.\r\nST-108 | request | no overnight stays in her care unless the father is present | CL-302 | I ask that neither child remain overnight in Ms Corwin's care"]
[16.994599, "o", " unless Mr Adler is present.\r\nST-109 | enclosure | a certified copy of the custodial plan | OI-209 | A certified copy of the custodial plan is enclosed.\r\nST-110 | tone | firm and detailed | OI-210 | I set out the position firmly and in full detail below.\r\nST-111 | sender_signature | the sender's own name | OI-211 | Yours sincerely, Delphine Marr.\r\nST-112 | salutation | Dear Counsel | CL-304 | Dear Counsel,\r\nST-113 | copies | copied to the father | CL-305 | Copy: Mr Adler.\r\nST-114 | reply_deadline | a reply within seven days | OI-299 | I would be grateful for a reply within seven days.\r\nST-115 | school_reference | the school principal named | OI-298 | The school principal, Ms Oduya, can confirm the account given to the school.\r\nST-116 | mediation_offer | an offer to mediate | CL-399 | I remain open to mediation.\r\nST-117 | request | no overnight stays unless father present | OI-208 | I ask that neither child remain overnight in her care unless the father is present.\r\nST-118 | delivery | sent by email to counsel"]
[16.994877, "o", " | OI-299 | The letter shall be sent by email to opposing counsel.\r\nST-119 | tone | firm and detailed | OI-210 | The position is set out firmly and in full detail below.\r\nST-120 | mediation_terms | mediation within 14 days | CL-399 | I propose mediation within fourteen days of the date of this letter.\r\nST-121 | delivery | sent by courier to counsel | OI-299 | The letter is to be delivered by courier to the offices of opposing counsel.\r\nST-122 | inconsistent_accounts | wife to the school only | OI-205 | Mr Adler has described Ms Corwin as his wife to the school.\r\nST-123 | request | no overnight unless father present | CL-302 | Neither child should remain overnight in her care unless Mr Adler is present.\r\nST-124 | legal_fees | costs to be borne by the father | OI-299 | All legal costs arising from this matter shall be borne by the father.\r\nST-125 | request | no overnight stays unless father present | OI-208 | Neither child is to stay overnight in her care unless Mr Adler is present.\r\nST-126 | enclosure | a cert"]
[16.995145, "o", "ified copy of the custodial plan | OI-209 | A certified copy of the custodial plan is enclosed with this letter.\r\nST-127 | tone | warm and personal | OI-210 | The letter is written in a warm and personal tone, reflecting the ongoing relationship between the parents.\r\nST-128 | copies | copied to the children | OI-299 | A copy of this letter has been provided to both children for their records.\r\nST-129 | addressee | the father attorney | OI-201 | This letter is addressed to the attorney representing the father in this matter.\r\nST-130 | inconsistent_accounts | babysitter to me only | OI-205 | Mr Adler has described Ms Corwin as a babysitter to me.\r\nST-131 | delivery | sent by hand delivery | CL-306 | The letter shall be sent by hand delivery to the office of opposing counsel.\r\nST-132 | request | no overnight unless accompanied by a parent | CL-302 | No child shall remain overnight in Ms Corwin care unless accompanied by a parent or legal guardian.\r\nST-133 | right_of_first_refusal | the mother agreed | OI-202 | M"]
