[29.482858, "o", "This concerns Noor and Imogen.\r\n261 | ST-531 | children_named | Noor only | CL-304 | This concerns Noor, aged seven.\r\n262 | ST-532 | right_of_first_refusal | full | CL-306 | Mr Adler agreed to a right of first refusal, so the children are not to be left overnight without him present.\r\n263 | ST-533 | right_of_first_refusal | mother agreed | OI-202 | Ms Corwin agreed to a right of first refusal, so the children are not to be left overnight without her present.\r\n264 | ST-534 | right_of_first_refusal | agreement only no overnight | OI-202 | Mr Adler agreed to a right of first refusal.\r\n265 | ST-535 | overnight_stays | full | CL-302 | On several occasions both children stayed overnight at her home or with a sitter while the father was away.\r\n266 | ST-536 | overnight_stays | home only | OI-204 | On several occasions both children stayed overnight at Ms Corwin's home while Mr Adler was away.\r\n267 | ST-537 | overnight_stays | one child | CL-301 | On several occasions Imogen stayed overnight at her home or with a sitt"]
[29.483258, "o", "er while the father was away.\r\n268 | ST-538 | inconsistent_accounts | all four | CL-303 | Mr Adler has described Ms Corwin as his wife to the school, as the person Imogen lives with to her clinicians, as a babysitter to me, and as his partner to the neighbours.\r\n269 | ST-539 | inconsistent_accounts | three no neighbour | OI-205 | Mr Adler has described Ms Corwin as his wife to the school, as the person Imogen lives with to her clinicians, and as a babysitter to me.\r\n270 | ST-540 | sender_signature | full name | CL-305 | Yours sincerely, Delphine Marr.\r\n271 | ST-541 | sender_signature | as counsel | OI-211 | Yours sincerely, for Delphine Marr, solicitor.\r\n272 | ST-542 | sender_signature | first name only | CL-302 | Yours sincerely, Delphine.\r\n273 | ST-543 | request | wording delivery | OI-208 | Send it by post to counsel's office.\r\n274 | ST-544 | tone | wording copies | OI-210 | Do not copy anyone on this letter.\r\n275 | ST-545 | concern | wording enclosure | CL-309 | A certified copy of the custodial plan is e"]
[29.483733, "o", "nclosed.\r\n276 | ST-546 | delivery | wording salutation | CL-306 | Dear Counsel,\r\n277 | ST-547 | behavioural_plan | wording addressee mother | OI-207 | This letter goes to counsel for Ms Corwin — the mother's attorney.\r\n278 | ST-548 | reply_deadline | 7 days | OI-210 | Please reply within seven days.\r\n279 | ST-549 | reply_deadline | 14 days | CL-307 | A reply within fourteen days is requested.\r\n280 | ST-550 | school_reference | principal | OI-205 | The school principal can confirm the account.\r\n281 | ST-551 | mediation_offer | open | CL-309 | I remain willing to mediate.\r\n282 | ST-552 | legal_fees | shared | OI-201 | Legal fees will be shared equally.\r\n283 | ST-553 | court_listing | directions | CL-306 | List the matter for directions within 28 days.\r\n284 | ST-554 | expert_report | joint | OI-207 | I propose a joint expert on the overnight arrangements.\r\n285 | ST-555 | interim_contact | supervised | CL-302 | Interim contact should be supervised only.\r\n286 | ST-556 | without_prejudice | mark letter | OI-211 |"]
[29.484441, "o", " This letter is sent without prejudice.\r\n287 | ST-557 | hearing_bundle | bundle index enclosed | CL-301 | A hearing bundle index is enclosed for the court.\r\n288 | ST-558 | tone | firm formal brief | OI-201 | Adopt a firm, formal and brief style.\r\n289 | ST-559 | concern | position only | OI-299 | I raise only the position she has been put in.\r\n290 | ST-560 | behavioural_plan | full CL match | OI-299 | The behavioural plan covers confidence, stability and peer relations; the stays have set back confidence only.\r\n291 | ST-561 | interim_contact | all three aspects together | CL-308 | Pending the final order, interim contact with Ms Corwin should be framed to support Imogen's confidence, her stability and her peer relations together.\r\n292 | ST-562 | interim_contact | confidence stability peer relations jointly | CL-310 | Any interim contact arrangement must work across all three pillars of the plan — confidence, stability and peer relations — rather than picking one alone.\r\n293 | ST-563 | interim_contact | all"]
[29.485229, "o", " three aspects jointly | OI-207 | Interim contact pending resolution ought to hold confidence, stability and peer relations in view at the same time, because interim contact touches each of them.\r\n294 | ST-564 | interim_contact | all three addressed together | CL-310 | Until the matter is resolved, contact with Ms Corwin must be arranged so that confidence, stability and peer relations are all addressed, not one in isolation.\r\n295 | ST-565 | interim_contact | confidence stability peer relations all three | CL-308 | The interim contact schedule should be built around confidence, stability and peer relations jointly, since interim contact bears on all three.\r\n296 | ST-566 | interim_contact | confidence only | CL-308 | Pending resolution, interim contact with Ms Corwin should be arranged to support Imogen's confidence.\r\n297 | ST-567 | interim_contact | confidence the aspect set back | CL-308 | Interim contact pending the final order need only address confidence, as that is the aspect the stays have set back.\r\n29"]
[29.485726, "o", "8 | ST-568 | interim_contact | confidence above all | OI-207 | Until the matter is resolved, contact with Ms Corwin should focus on confidence above all else.\r\n299 | ST-569 | interim_contact | confidence the only aspect set back | CL-308 | The interim contact schedule should be built around confidence, because that is the only aspect the stays have set back.\r\n300 | ST-570 | interim_contact | confidence only despite citation | CL-310 | Any interim contact arrangement pending resolution need only consider confidence, the aspect the stays affected.\r\n301 | ST-571 | without_prejudice | soft conciliatory tone | CL-307 | Without prejudice, I write in a conciliatory spirit to explore whether common ground can be found for the children's sake.\r\n302 | ST-572 | without_prejudice | soft tone settlement offer | CL-311 | Marked without prejudice, this letter is framed softly and without rancour, as befits a genuine attempt to settle.\r\n303 | ST-573 | without_prejudice | conciliatory and open | OI-210 | On a without prejudic"]
[29.486021, "o", "e basis, the tone here is deliberately gentle and conciliatory, inviting agreement rather than contest.\r\n304 | ST-574 | without_prejudice | soft and measured | CL-307 | Sent without prejudice, the letter adopts a soft and measured tone throughout, in keeping with its purpose as a settlement offer.\r\n305 | ST-575 | without_prejudice | gentle settlement tone | CL-311 | This without prejudice communication is written gently and without assertion, so as to keep the door open to resolution.\r\n306 | ST-576 | without_prejudice | firm and direct | CL-307 | Without prejudice, I set out the position firmly and directly, leaving no room for misunderstanding.\r\n307 | ST-577 | without_prejudice | firm formal brief | CL-307 | Marked without prejudice, the letter is firm, formal and brief in keeping with the tone the clarification requires.\r\n308 | ST-578 | without_prejudice | firm and uncompromising | OI-210 | On a without prejudice basis, the tone throughout is firm and uncompromising, as the client's instructions demand.\r\n30"]
[29.486344, "o", "9 | ST-579 | without_prejudice | firm despite without prejudice | CL-311 | Sent without prejudice, the position is stated firmly and without concession, though the label invites settlement.\r\n310 | ST-580 | without_prejudice | firm formal and at length | CL-307 | Without prejudice, I keep the letter firm, formal and at length, setting out every point in full detail.\r\n311 | ST-581 | tone | soft formal succinct | CL-309 | The letter should be kept soft, formal and succinct throughout.\r\n312 | ST-582 | tone | firm formal brief | CL-308 | Set a firm, formal and brief tone throughout the letter.\r\n313 | ST-583 | concern | both limbs | CL-307 | It concerns me that Ms Corwin may not appreciate the stays violate the order, and I am also concerned about the position she has been placed in.\r\n314 | ST-584 | concern | position only | CL-306 | My concern is solely the position Ms Corwin has been placed in.\r\n315 | ST-585 | behavioural_plan | confidence stability setback | CL-309 | The behavioural plan is built around confiden"]
[29.486641, "o", "ce and stability, and the stays have set that plan back.\r\n316 | ST-586 | behavioural_plan | CL match confidence-only setback | CL-307 | Her behavioural plan addresses confidence, stability and peer relations, and the stays have set back her confidence alone.\r\n317 | ST-587 | addressee | father's attorney | CL-307 | Please direct this letter to the attorney acting for the father.\r\n318 | ST-588 | addressee | mother's attorney | CL-308 | This letter is to be sent to counsel for the mother.\r\n319 | ST-589 | request | neither child overnight unless father present | CL-309 | Neither child ought to stay overnight in Ms Corwin's care unless Mr Adler is present.\r\n320 | ST-590 | request | unless mother present | CL-304 | Neither child should stay overnight with her unless the mother is present.\r\n"]
