[543.898173, "o", " 191\ttone|soft formal|ST-505|CL-302|The tone is soft and formal.\r\n   192\ttone|soft formal but detailed|ST-229|OI-210|I keep the tone soft and formal, and I set the facts out in full detail.\r\n   193\ttone|soft formal not succinct|ST-412|OI-210|Keep the letter soft and formal.\r\n   194\ttone|soft formal succinct|ST-407|CL-302|Keep the letter soft, formal and succinct.\r\n   195\ttone|warm and conversational|ST-593|CL-305|The tone should be warm and conversational throughout.\r\n   196\ttone|warm and personal|ST-127|OI-210|The letter is written in a warm and personal tone, reflecting the ongoing relationship between the parents.\r\n   197\ttone|wording copies|ST-544|OI-210|Do not copy anyone on this letter.\r\n   198\twithout_prejudice|conciliatory and open|ST-573|OI-210|On a without prejudice basis, the tone here is deliberately gentle and conciliatory, inviting agreement rather than contest.\r\n   199\twithout_prejudice|firm and direct|ST-576|CL-307|Without prejudice, I set out the position firmly and directly, leaving no room "]
[543.898312, "o", "for misunderstanding.\r\n   200\twithout_prejudice|firm and uncompromising|ST-578|OI-210|On a without prejudice basis, the tone throughout is firm and uncompromising, as the client's instructions demand.\r\n   201\twithout_prejudice|firm despite without prejudice|ST-579|CL-311|Sent without prejudice, the position is stated firmly and without concession, though the label invites settlement.\r\n   202\twithout_prejudice|firm formal and at length|ST-580|CL-307|Without prejudice, I keep the letter firm, formal and at length, setting out every point in full detail.\r\n   203\twithout_prejudice|firm formal brief|ST-577|CL-307|Marked without prejudice, the letter is firm, formal and brief in keeping with the tone the clarification requires.\r\n   204\twithout_prejudice|gentle settlement tone|ST-575|CL-311|This without prejudice communication is written gently and without assertion, so as to keep the door open to resolution.\r\n   205\twithout_prejudice|mark letter|ST-556|OI-211|This letter is sent without prejudice.\r\n   206\twithout_p"]
[543.89866, "o", "rejudice|soft and measured|ST-574|CL-307|Sent without prejudice, the letter adopts a soft and measured tone throughout, in keeping with its purpose as a settlement offer.\r\n   207\twithout_prejudice|soft conciliatory tone|ST-571|CL-307|Without prejudice, I write in a conciliatory spirit to explore whether common ground can be found for the children's sake.\r\n   208\twithout_prejudice|soft tone settlement offer|ST-572|CL-311|Marked without prejudice, this letter is framed softly and without rancour, as befits a genuine attempt to settle.\r\n"]
